  "verified_invariants": [
    "persistent friction state resets at trajectory-segment boundaries",
    "candidate innovation is supervised separately from update authority",
    "counterfactual information is estimated across multiple friction perturbation scales",
    "cross-scale inconsistency can discount local observability authority",
    "candidate-vs-prior residual evidence is an asymmetric veto",
    "inverse-dynamics agreement spans 0 to 1 and can supply an identifiability-weighted veto",
    "excitation-proxy ablation keeps raw features and changes the authority source rather than the full estimator path",
    "no-identifiability ablation does not leak learned information through the agreement veto",
    "final point output remains inside the conditional physical support",
    "point-model tuning does not optimize UQ-only information_beta",
    "hyperparameter sensitivity uses locked validation endpoints and no test labels",
    "primary ablations use explicit semantic specifications"
  ],
